Syntax: television <person>

Telepathic vision allows a skilled psionicist to perceive the world
through another person's senses. By focusing on a specific individual
anywhere in the world, the psionicist can momentarily see what they
see, perceiving their surroundings as if standing in their place.

The power requires intense concentration to establish the mental link.
Upon success, the psionicist receives a brief glimpse of the target's
location, seeing the room and its contents exactly as the target would.
The vision is fleeting - just enough to understand where someone is
and what surrounds them.

This is an advanced power that requires significant mastery of psionics
before it can be learned. The mental effort required is substantial,
consuming considerable mana. If the psionicist fails to establish a
proper mental connection, they learn nothing and the mana is still
expended.

Certain powerful beings shield their minds from such intrusion. Immortals
in particular cannot be targeted by this power - their minds are simply
too vast and alien for a mortal psionicist to perceive through.
Additionally, the power cannot perceive into certain protected locations.

The power cannot be used while focusing your mind, as the concentration
required for mind focus precludes external projection.

